> laplace solve y'' - 2*y' + y = 0, y(0)=1, y'(0)=0
y'' - 2*y' + y = 0, y(0) = 1, y'(0) = 0
  transformed: (s^2 - 2s + 1)Y(s) - (s - 2) = 0
  Y(s) = (s - 2)/(s - 1)^2
  y(t) = (1 - t)*e^t    for t >= 0
  poles of Y: 1 (double)
  check: residual of the equation at 201 points of [0, 10]: max 2.9e-11; initial values hold (max difference 0)
  check: a numeric solution (RK4, h = 1/1000) agrees at 20 points of [0, 10]: max difference 2.3e-08
> laplace solve y'' + y = sin(t), y(0)=0, y'(0)=0
y'' + y = sin(t), y(0) = 0, y'(0) = 0
  transformed: (s^2 + 1)Y(s) = 1/(s^2 + 1)
  Y(s) = 1/(s^2 + 1)^2
  y(t) = -t*cos(t)/2 + sin(t)/2    for t >= 0
  poles of Y: +-i (double)
  check: residual of the equation at 201 points of [0, 10]: max 7.8e-16; initial values hold (max difference 0)
  check: a numeric solution (RK4, h = 1/1000) agrees at 20 points of [0, 10]: max difference 1.5e-13
> laplace solve y' - y = exp(t), y(0)=0
y' - y = exp(t), y(0) = 0
  transformed: (s - 1)Y(s) = 1/(s - 1)
  Y(s) = 1/(s - 1)^2
  y(t) = t*e^t    for t >= 0
  poles of Y: 1 (double)
  check: residual of the equation at 201 points of [0, 10]: max 1.3e-11; initial values hold (max difference 0)
  check: a numeric solution (RK4, h = 1/1000) agrees at 20 points of [0, 10]: max difference 1.3e-08
> laplace solve y'' + 2*y' + 5*y = dirac(t), y(0)=0, y'(0)=0
y'' + 2*y' + 5*y = dirac(t), y(0) = 0, y'(0) = 0
  transformed: (s^2 + 2s + 5)Y(s) = 1
  Y(s) = 1/(s^2 + 2s + 5)
  y(t) = e^(-t)*sin(2t)/2    for t >= 0
  poles of Y: -1 +- 2i
